From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 05:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: take down and restore the partners of a driver owner
 interface
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

027 removes the BSSes of other interfaces that run on the driver of an
interface that is being removed or disabled, but only when that
interface's first BSS is a plain BSS. An interface whose first BSS is
itself an AP MLD link kept upstream's semantics: hostapd_cleanup_driver()
sees the driver shared with the partner links, removes only the departing
link and leaves the driver, its nl80211 context and the netdev to them.

On prplOS with pWHM that is the common topology. The MLD netdev is the
main VAP of the radio that came up first (wlan0.1), and the first BSSes
or secondary BSSes of the other radios are links of it that borrow its
context. When pWHM re-applies such a radio with a configuration in which
that VAP is no longer an AP MLD link, it sends REMOVE for the owner
interface and ADDs the new configuration, and the ADD initializes a new
driver on the same netdev while the surviving context still holds the
wdev's management frame registrations:

  hostapd: Remove interface 'wlan0.1_link0'
  hostapd: Configuration file: /tmp/wlan0_hapd.conf (phy wlan0) --> new PHY
  hostapd: nl80211: kernel reports: Match already configured
  hostapd: nl80211: Could not configure driver mode
  hostapd: nl80211 driver initialization failed.
  hostapd: Adding interface bss_config=wlan0 failed
  wld: wlan0: warm apply failed to add iface conf => restart to recover

cfg80211_mlme_register_mgmt() rejects a match that another socket has
already registered on the wdev with -EALREADY, and pWHM recovers with a
full hostapd restart. If instead the last partner link goes away later,
the driver stays allocated with drv->ctx pointing at a freed
hostapd_data and the next interface-down event on that netdev is
delivered to it.

Drop the AP MLD exclusion in hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers(): what
matters is that the driver behind bss[0] was created by this interface,
which hapd->drv_owner_iface records. The partners are taken down before
the driver cleanup, so that hostapd_cleanup_driver() finds the driver
unshared, deinitializes it and releases the netdev, and the ADD gets a
fresh driver.

The partners are not lost. A borrower is an AP MLD link by construction
(only hostapd_setup_bss() and driver_init() borrow a context, both for
an mld_ap BSS), and the owner may be an AP MLD link or a plain BSS whose
interface hosts the first links of other AP MLDs, as wlan2.1 does for
the guest and backhaul MLDs once it has left the private MLD. So the
decision for a secondary partner is taken per partner, not per owner:

- A partner that is the first BSS of its interface is disabled, keeping
  its configuration and control sockets. For an AP MLD owner it is
  also marked mld_partner_disabled.
- A partner that is a secondary BSS of a running interface and an AP
  MLD link is taken down like hostapd_remove_bss() does, but its
  configuration is parked on that interface, together with the
  identity the BSS had: its link ID (and so the control socket name
  <mld>_link<N>), its link address, its AP MLD (conf->iface) and its
  radio (the interface's phy). Whether the owner is an AP MLD link or
  a plain BSS does not matter here.
- A plain partner, should one exist, is removed as 027 does.

When a later interface setup completes while such recovery is pending,
hostapd_mld_reattach_partners() runs from the event loop and restores
every partner whose own AP MLD has a running first BSS with a driver
again: a marked interface is enabled, and driver_init() borrows the new
context as before; a parked BSS is added back to its interface the way
"ADD bss_config=" adds a BSS, with hostapd_setup_bss(first = 0) so that,
unlike the -1 of that command, the link is added to the driver and to
the AP MLD, and under its previous link ID when the AP MLD has not
reused it. The re-add counts as done only once the link add and the BSS
setup succeeded; otherwise the BSS stays parked. So a REMOVE/ADD of the
owner alone, with the same AP MLD, restores all of its partners without
any controller action, and moving one AP out of and back into an AP MLD
leaves the other AP MLDs with all of their links (pWHM removes and
re-adds the radio whose VAP changes; its guest and backhaul links on the
other radios were lost before).

A partner supplied again meanwhile is not duplicated: once an ADD is
accepted for an interface on the same phy with a BSS of the same AP
MLD, or with a BSS with the same link address on any phy, the parked
copy is dropped, also when the controller gets a separate hostapd_iface
for it because its configuration starts with an AP MLD link. A
successful reload of an interface, from its configuration file
(RELOAD_CONFIG) or in memory (RELOAD), accepts the complete set of
BSSes the interface then has and drops the parked BSSes it omits or
lists again; RELOAD_BSS is scoped to its BSS and drops only a parked
copy of that one. A failed reload leaves the parked state alone.

An explicit DISABLE of the interface, including one that is already
down, or a REMOVE of the interface cancels its pending recovery. A
parked BSS is addressed by the control socket name it had: "REMOVE
<mld>_link<N>" drops exactly that one. A bare "REMOVE <mld>" that
matches no live interface or BSS drops the parked BSS of that AP MLD if
there is exactly one and fails otherwise, since the name shared by the
links of an AP MLD does not say which radio is meant; the live
interfaces and BSSes are searched first, as before, so a parked BSS
never stands in for a live one or the other way round. The timer is
cancelled once nothing is pending anywhere. The eviction itself uses an
internal disable that does not cancel the recovery.

If the owner comes back as a plain BSS, or with another AP MLD, the
partners' configurations no longer describe a link that can exist: they
stay down or parked until the controller re-applies them. pWHM does so
in the flows that cause such a re-ADD, since the change of the primary
link marks the configured neighbour links for an AP MLD configuration
refresh; a REMOVE of the partner interface then drops its parked BSSes.

For a plain owner the borrower selection, the teardown order, the
first-BSS partner handling, hostapd_remove_bss() and
hostapd_cleanup_driver() are unchanged; the configuration of a
secondary AP MLD link partner is now retained and its recovery is
pending instead of the partner being lost.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 624 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/ap/hostapd.h |  30 +++
 2 files changed, 647 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index d4e66426e2f5..9c378fbcb4af 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -70,6 +70,17 @@ static void hostapd_cleanup_unused_mlds(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces);
 static int hostapd_remove_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface, unsigned int idx);
 static void hostapd_interface_setup_failure_handler(void *eloop_ctx,
 						    void *timeout_ctx);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+static void hostapd_mld_reattach_partners(void *eloop_ctx, void *timeout_ctx);
+static bool hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces);
+static void hostapd_mld_revoke_recovery(struct hostapd_iface *iface);
+static void hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					const char *reason);
+static void hostapd_mld_drop_resupplied_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface);
+static void hostapd_mld_reconcile_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					     const char *bss);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+static int hostapd_disable_iface_int(struct hostapd_iface *hapd_iface);
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211AX
 static void hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handler(void *eloop_data,
 						 void *user_ctx);
@@ -297,6 +308,9 @@ int hostapd_reload_config(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 		hostapd_clear_old(iface);
 		for (j = 0; j < iface->num_bss; j++)
 			hostapd_reload_bss(iface->bss[j]);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+		hostapd_mld_reconcile_parked_bss(iface, NULL);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 		return 0;
 	}
 
@@ -373,6 +387,10 @@ int hostapd_reload_config(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 	}
 
 	hostapd_config_free(oldconf);
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	/* The file is the complete accepted set of BSSes of this interface */
+	hostapd_mld_reconcile_parked_bss(iface, NULL);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
 
 	return 0;
@@ -2830,6 +2848,24 @@ dfs_offload:
 	if (iface->interfaces && iface->interfaces->count > 1)
 		ieee802_11_set_beacons(iface);
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (iface->interfaces) {
+		/* A BSS this interface runs replaces a parked copy of it */
+		hostapd_mld_drop_resupplied_parked_bss(iface);
+		/* This interface may have given an AP MLD a first BSS with a
+		 * driver again; let the partners
+		 * hostapd_remove_drv_borrowers() took down borrow it. Do it
+		 * from the event loop, outside of this setup. */
+		if (hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(iface->interfaces)) {
+			eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+					     iface->interfaces, NULL);
+			eloop_register_timeout(0, 0,
+					       hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+					       iface->interfaces, NULL);
+		}
+	}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
 	return 0;
 
 fail:
@@ -3126,6 +3162,7 @@ void hostapd_interface_free(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
 	size_t j;
 	wpa_printf(MSG_DEBUG, "%s(%p)", __func__, iface);
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss(iface, "interface freed");
 	/* A BSS elsewhere that still names this interface as the owner of its
 	 * driver runs on a driver that was left alive by
 	 * hostapd_cleanup_driver(); nobody owns that driver any more. */
@@ -3546,6 +3583,518 @@ hostapd_interface_init_bss(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces, const char *phy,
 }
 
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+
+static bool hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces)
+{
+	size_t i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *iface = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		if (iface && (iface->mld_partner_disabled ||
+			      iface->num_mld_parked_bss))
+			return true;
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+
+/* Release the parked array once it is empty, and the recovery timer once
+ * nothing is pending anywhere. */
+static void hostapd_mld_parked_bss_changed(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
+{
+	if (iface->num_mld_parked_bss)
+		return;
+	os_free(iface->mld_parked_bss);
+	iface->mld_parked_bss = NULL;
+	if (iface->interfaces &&
+	    !hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(iface->interfaces))
+		eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+				     iface->interfaces, NULL);
+}
+
+
+/* Forget parked BSS idx of iface and free its configuration. */
+static void hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					    size_t idx, const char *reason)
+{
+	struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p = &iface->mld_parked_bss[idx];
+	size_t i;
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+		   "Drop parked BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u, BSSID " MACSTR
+		   ") of phy %s: %s",
+		   p->conf->iface, p->link_id, MAC2STR(p->bssid), iface->phy,
+		   reason);
+	hostapd_config_free_bss(p->conf);
+	iface->num_mld_parked_bss--;
+	for (i = idx; i < iface->num_mld_parked_bss; i++)
+		iface->mld_parked_bss[i] = iface->mld_parked_bss[i + 1];
+	hostapd_mld_parked_bss_changed(iface);
+}
+
+
+static void hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					const char *reason)
+{
+	while (iface->num_mld_parked_bss)
+		hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(
+			iface, iface->num_mld_parked_bss - 1, reason);
+}
+
+
+/* Keep a parked BSS record on iface. Frees the configuration if the record
+ * cannot be stored. */
+static void hostapd_mld_park_record(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+				    const struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p)
+{
+	struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *tmp;
+
+	tmp = os_realloc_array(iface->mld_parked_bss,
+			       iface->num_mld_parked_bss + 1, sizeof(*tmp));
+	if (!tmp) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+			   "Cannot park BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u): out of memory",
+			   p->conf->iface, p->link_id);
+		hostapd_config_free_bss(p->conf);
+		return;
+	}
+	iface->mld_parked_bss = tmp;
+	tmp[iface->num_mld_parked_bss++] = *p;
+}
+
+
+/* An explicit disable or removal of the interface cancels its pending
+ * automatic recovery: it stays down, and its parked BSSes are forgotten. */
+static void hostapd_mld_revoke_recovery(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
+{
+	if (!iface->mld_partner_disabled && !iface->num_mld_parked_bss)
+		return;
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+		   "Interface %s: cancel pending AP MLD partner recovery (%u parked BSS)",
+		   iface->phy, (unsigned int) iface->num_mld_parked_bss);
+	iface->mld_partner_disabled = 0;
+	hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss(iface, "recovery cancelled");
+	if (iface->interfaces &&
+	    !hostapd_mld_recovery_pending(iface->interfaces))
+		eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_mld_reattach_partners,
+				     iface->interfaces, NULL);
+}
+
+
+/* Take down secondary BSS idx of iface the way hostapd_remove_bss() does,
+ * but keep its configuration, with the identity the BSS had, for
+ * hostapd_mld_reattach_partners(). */
+static void hostapd_mld_park_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface, unsigned int idx,
+				 struct hostapd_iface *owner)
+{
+	struct hostapd_data *hapd = iface->bss[idx];
+	struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss p;
+	size_t i;
+
+	os_memset(&p, 0, sizeof(p));
+	p.conf = hapd->conf;
+	p.link_id = hapd->mld_link_id;
+	os_memcpy(p.bssid, hapd->own_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+		   "Park BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u, BSSID " MACSTR
+		   ") of interface %s: it uses the driver of %s that is being deinitialized",
+		   hapd->conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id,
+		   MAC2STR(hapd->own_addr), iface->bss[0]->conf->iface,
+		   owner->bss[0]->conf->iface);
+
+	/* As hostapd_remove_bss(), without hostapd_config_free_bss() */
+	hostapd_bss_deinit(hapd);
+	hapd->conf = NULL;
+	hostapd_mld_ref_dec(hapd->mld);
+	os_free(hapd);
+
+	iface->num_bss--;
+	for (i = idx; i < iface->num_bss; i++)
+		iface->bss[i] = iface->bss[i + 1];
+	iface->conf->num_bss--;
+	for (i = idx; i < iface->conf->num_bss; i++)
+		iface->conf->bss[i] = iface->conf->bss[i + 1];
+
+	hostapd_mld_park_record(iface, &p);
+}
+
+
+static struct hostapd_data *
+hostapd_mld_running_first_bss(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces,
+			      const char *mld_name)
+{
+	size_t i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->mld_count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_mld *mld = interfaces->mld[i];
+
+		if (mld && os_strcmp(mld->name, mld_name) == 0 && mld->fbss &&
+		    mld->fbss->drv_priv &&
+		    mld->fbss->iface->state == HAPD_IFACE_ENABLED)
+			return mld->fbss;
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+
+
+static bool hostapd_mld_link_id_in_use(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces,
+				       struct hostapd_mld *mld, u8 link_id)
+{
+	size_t i, j;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *iface = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		for (j = 0; iface && j < iface->num_bss; j++) {
+			if (iface->bss[j]->mld == mld &&
+			    iface->bss[j]->mld_link_id == link_id)
+				return true;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+
+/* Whether a live BSS describes the same link as parked BSS p of iface: the
+ * same AP MLD on the same phy, or the same link address. The controller may
+ * have supplied it again to any interface of the phy, including a separate
+ * interface it gets when its configuration starts with an AP MLD link. */
+static bool hostapd_mld_parked_bss_is_live(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces,
+					   struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					   const struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p)
+{
+	size_t i, j;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *other = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		for (j = 0; other && j < other->num_bss; j++) {
+			struct hostapd_data *hapd = other->bss[j];
+
+			if (!hapd->conf->mld_ap)
+				continue;
+			if (os_strcmp(other->phy, iface->phy) == 0 &&
+			    os_strcmp(hapd->conf->iface, p->conf->iface) == 0)
+				return true;
+			if (!is_zero_ether_addr(p->bssid) &&
+			    (ether_addr_equal(hapd->own_addr, p->bssid) ||
+			     ether_addr_equal(hapd->conf->bssid, p->bssid)))
+				return true;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return false;
+}
+
+
+/* A BSS supplied again while its previous instance is parked replaces the
+ * parked copy. Called once an interface has set up its BSSes. */
+static void hostapd_mld_drop_resupplied_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface)
+{
+	struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces = iface->interfaces;
+	size_t i, k;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *other = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		if (!other)
+			continue;
+		for (k = other->num_mld_parked_bss; k > 0; k--) {
+			if (hostapd_mld_parked_bss_is_live(
+				    interfaces, other,
+				    &other->mld_parked_bss[k - 1]))
+				hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(
+					other, k - 1, "supplied again");
+		}
+	}
+}
+
+
+/* Reconcile the parked BSSes of iface after a successful reload. A reload of
+ * the whole interface (bss == NULL) accepts iface->conf as its complete set
+ * of BSSes: a parked BSS it lists is a duplicate of a live BSS, one it omits
+ * was deleted by the controller; both are dropped. A reload of one BSS is
+ * scoped to that BSS and drops only a parked copy of it. */
+static void hostapd_mld_reconcile_parked_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+					     const char *bss)
+{
+	size_t j, k;
+
+	for (k = iface->num_mld_parked_bss; k > 0; k--) {
+		struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p = &iface->mld_parked_bss[k - 1];
+		bool listed = false;
+
+		if (bss) {
+			if (os_strcmp(p->conf->iface, bss) == 0)
+				hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(
+					iface, k - 1, "configured again");
+			continue;
+		}
+		for (j = 0; j < iface->conf->num_bss; j++) {
+			if (os_strcmp(iface->conf->bss[j]->iface,
+				      p->conf->iface) == 0)
+				listed = true;
+		}
+		hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(
+			iface, k - 1, listed ? "configured again" :
+			"not in the reloaded configuration");
+	}
+}
+
+
+/* Parse "<mld>_link<N>" into <mld> and N; returns N, or -1 for a bare name. */
+static int hostapd_mld_parse_link_sock_name(const char *buf, char *name,
+					    size_t name_len)
+{
+	const char *pos = NULL, *q = buf;
+	char *end;
+	long id;
+
+	while ((q = os_strstr(q, "_" WPA_CTRL_IFACE_LINK_NAME)))
+		pos = q++;
+	if (!pos || pos == buf || (size_t) (pos - buf) >= name_len)
+		return -1;
+	q = pos + 1 + os_strlen(WPA_CTRL_IFACE_LINK_NAME);
+	if (*q < '0' || *q > '9')
+		return -1;
+	id = strtol(q, &end, 10);
+	if (*end || id < 0 || id >= MAX_NUM_MLD_LINKS)
+		return -1;
+	os_memcpy(name, buf, pos - buf);
+	name[pos - buf] = '\0';
+	return (int) id;
+}
+
+
+/* "REMOVE <mld>_link<N>", the control socket name the BSS had, drops exactly
+ * the parked BSS that was link N of AP MLD <mld>. A bare "REMOVE <mld>" that
+ * matched no live interface or BSS drops the parked BSS of that AP MLD if
+ * there is exactly one; with several it fails, since a name shared by the
+ * links of an AP MLD does not say which radio is meant. */
+static int hostapd_mld_remove_parked_bss(struct hapd_interfaces *interfaces,
+					 const char *buf)
+{
+	struct hostapd_iface *match_iface = NULL;
+	char name[IFNAMSIZ + 1];
+	int link_id, matches = 0;
+	size_t i, k, match_idx = 0;
+
+	link_id = hostapd_mld_parse_link_sock_name(buf, name, sizeof(name));
+
+	for (i = 0; i < interfaces->count; i++) {
+		struct hostapd_iface *iface = interfaces->iface[i];
+
+		if (!iface)
+			continue;
+		for (k = iface->num_mld_parked_bss; k > 0; k--) {
+			struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p =
+				&iface->mld_parked_bss[k - 1];
+
+			if (link_id >= 0 ? (p->link_id != link_id ||
+					    os_strcmp(p->conf->iface, name)) :
+			    os_strcmp(p->conf->iface, buf))
+				continue;
+			matches++;
+			match_iface = iface;
+			match_idx = k - 1;
+		}
+	}
+
+	if (matches != 1) {
+		if (matches)
+			wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+				   "Remove parked BSS '%s': ambiguous, %d parked links of that AP MLD; use REMOVE %s_%s<N>",
+				   buf, matches, buf, WPA_CTRL_IFACE_LINK_NAME);
+		return -1;
+	}
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "Remove parked BSS '%s'", buf);
+	hostapd_mld_drop_parked_bss_idx(match_iface, match_idx, "REMOVE");
+	return 0;
+}
+
+
+/* Add parked BSS p back to its running interface the way "ADD bss_config="
+ * adds a BSS to an existing interface, as a non-first link of its AP MLD
+ * whose running first BSS is fbss. Returns 0 once the link was added to the
+ * driver and the BSS set up; p->conf then belongs to iface. Otherwise the BSS
+ * is not added, p->conf is untouched and -1 is returned. */
+static int hostapd_mld_unpark_bss(struct hostapd_iface *iface,
+				  const struct hostapd_mld_parked_bss *p,
+				  struct hostapd_data *fbss)
+{
+	struct hostapd_bss_config *conf = p->conf;
+	struct hostapd_bss_config **tmp_conf;
+	struct hostapd_data **tmp_bss, *hapd;
+	struct hostapd_mld *mld;
+
+	tmp_conf = os_realloc_array(iface->conf->bss, iface->conf->num_bss + 1,
+				    sizeof(*tmp_conf));
+	if (tmp_conf)
+		iface->conf->bss = tmp_conf;
+	tmp_bss = os_realloc_array(iface->bss, iface->num_bss + 1,
+				   sizeof(*tmp_bss));
+	if (tmp_bss)
+		iface->bss = tmp_bss;
+	if (!tmp_conf || !tmp_bss)
+		return -1;
+
+	iface->conf->bss[iface->conf->num_bss++] = conf;
+	hapd = hostapd_alloc_bss_data(iface, iface->conf, conf);
+	if (!hapd) {
+		iface->conf->num_bss--;
+		return -1;
+	}
+	iface->bss[iface->num_bss++] = hapd;
+	hapd->msg_ctx = hapd;
+	hostapd_bss_setup_multi_link(hapd, iface->interfaces);
+	mld = hapd->mld;
+	if (!mld || hostapd_mld_get_first_bss(hapd) != fbss) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+			   "Cannot re-add BSS '%s': it did not join the AP MLD of %s",
+			   conf->iface, fbss->conf->iface);
+		goto fail;
+	}
+
+	/* Keep the link ID the BSS had, so that it comes back under its
+	 * previous control socket name, unless the AP MLD reused it. */
+	if (p->link_id < MAX_NUM_MLD_LINKS &&
+	    !hostapd_mld_link_id_in_use(iface->interfaces, mld, p->link_id)) {
+		if (mld->next_link_id == hapd->mld_link_id + 1)
+			mld->next_link_id--;
+		hapd->mld_link_id = p->link_id;
+		if (mld->next_link_id <= p->link_id)
+			mld->next_link_id = p->link_id + 1;
+	}
+
+	hapd->driver = iface->bss[0]->driver;
+	hapd->drv_priv = iface->bss[0]->drv_priv;
+	hapd->drv_owner_iface = iface->bss[0]->drv_owner_iface;
+	os_memcpy(hapd->own_addr, iface->bss[0]->own_addr, ETH_ALEN);
+
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+		   "Re-add BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u) to interface %s: its AP MLD has a first BSS with a driver again",
+		   conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id, iface->bss[0]->conf->iface);
+	/* first = 0: a non-first BSS of the interface. hostapd_setup_bss()
+	 * makes it borrow the driver context of the first BSS of its AP MLD
+	 * and, unlike the -1 of "ADD bss_config=", adds the link to the driver
+	 * and to the AP MLD. */
+	if (start_ctrl_iface_bss(hapd) < 0 || hostapd_setup_bss(hapd, 0, true)) {
+		wpa_printf(MSG_WARNING,
+			   "Failed to re-add BSS '%s' (AP MLD link %u) to interface %s: it stays parked",
+			   conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id,
+			   iface->bss[0]->conf->iface);
+		goto fail;
+	}
+	wpa_printf(MSG_INFO, "Re-added BSS '%s' as AP MLD link %u of interface %s",
+		   conf->iface, hapd->mld_link_id, iface->bss[0]->conf->iface);
+	hostapd_owe_update_trans(iface);
+	return 0;
+
+fail:
+	hostapd_bss_link_deinit(hapd);
+	hostapd_cleanup(hapd);
+	iface->bss[--iface->num_bss] = NULL;
+	iface->conf->num_bss--;
+	hapd->conf = NULL;
+	hostapd_mld_ref_dec(hapd->mld);
+	os_free(hapd);
+	return -1;
+}
